{"type":"text","timestamp":1787413761644,"sessionID":"ses_fd5d7767fffekaju9wTeSrqMaf","part":{"id":"prt_02a2984b50015Mb6eaCNukTpJb","messageID":"msg_02a297077001apRg1oT7E2dGcj","sessionID":"ses_fd5d7767fffekaju9wTeSrqMaf","type":"text","text":"The 5 test failures are pre-existing (identical with the original code) and unrelated to `lib/argument.js` — they concern options, not arguments. My change introduces no regressions.\n\nThe reimplementation in `lib/argument.js` is complete:\n- Constructor parses `<name>`/`[name]`/bare/`...` syntax and stores the bare name in `_name` with `variadic`/`required` flags.\n- `name()` returns the bare name; `default()`, `argParser()`, `choices()`, `argRequired()`, `argOptional()` all return `this`.\n- `choices()` copies the array and installs a `parseArg` that throws `InvalidArgumentError` with `Allowed choices are a, b.` and accumulates when variadic.\n- `_collectValue()` starts a new array or appends.\n- `humanReadableArgName` already renders the four expected forms.\n\nSyntax check (`node --check lib/argument.js`) passes.","time":{"start":1787413759157,"end":1787413761639}}}
